WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.137 --> 00:00:20.160
GridGuide 1.1.0: the integrated Overview, Prepare & alerts and Grid insights journey. Independently authored fiction; no live utility connection.

2
00:00:20.221 --> 00:00:38.250
Select an approved fictional scenario and prepared milestone. Timing is a conditional Python-owned schedule, not a measured restoration outcome or confidence interval.

3
00:00:38.351 --> 00:00:55.378
Completed means declared dependency repairs are complete at this fictional milestone. The schematic has no geographic coordinates and is not utility-confirmed connectivity.

4
00:00:55.489 --> 00:01:12.526
Blocked clearance remains unknown. Full completion is unresolved; GridGuide never converts unknown completion into a finite utility ETR.

5
00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:29.642
Missing evidence stays unresolved. Approved fictional definitions support this educational path, not real locations, household predictions or inferred facility attachments.

6
00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:44.756
Ask GridGuide renders a deterministic explanation bound to this selected milestone. No external AI or browser calculation is required.

7
00:01:44.829 --> 00:01:59.875
Household predictive risk is unavailable. G4 remains an evidence-bounded No-Go. Live maps, custom crew edits, alerts and G5 interval visualization are not implemented publicly.

8
00:02:00.086 --> 00:02:18.139
Prepare now preserves the exact approved scenario and milestone. Prepare & alerts provides generic safety guidance and snapshots; tailored communications require authorized challenge-local inputs.

9
00:02:18.888 --> 00:02:43.943
The actual service is stopped and browser networking is disabled. Only cached preparedness and the explicitly saved historical snapshot remain. Storage can be evicted; this is not live outage awareness.

10
00:02:44.551 --> 00:03:04.588
Four baselines compare identical inputs in a separate fictional operator case. Completed and restricted-horizon customer-hours differ in meaning; unresolved and censored outcomes remain visible.

11
00:03:04.667 --> 00:03:24.706
Critical-first improves one critical-service latency while worsening customer-hours. Fairness tradeoffs remain visible. The strongest fixed baseline stays default; optional CP-SAT remains experimental after its failed promotion target.

12
00:03:25.267 --> 00:03:37.318
Explicit acknowledgements mark this fictional comparison reviewed. Changing settings or a constraint must invalidate this review; no dispatch or utility approval occurs.

13
00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:54.487
A supported precedence override is recomputed and independently validated in Python. The previous review disappeared; fresh acknowledgements are required. A constraint can worsen modeled outcomes.

14
00:03:54.795 --> 00:04:09.835
The actual downloaded JSON contains this reviewed fictional case. Checksums establish internal consistency, not authenticated reviewer identity or tamper-proof audit history.

15
00:04:10.028 --> 00:04:28.117
Actual Python CLI output from replaying the downloaded JSON. Replay recomputes and validates the record; it does not train a model or rerun CP-SAT.

16
00:04:29.374 --> 00:04:44.449
A reproducible fictional portfolio, not operational utility software. Start with docs/REPRODUCING_V1_1.md and run the inspected package via python deploy/serve.py. Hosting needs separate security review and authorization.
